# UI Widget Conventions

Always use the shared widgets from `lib/core/widgets/` instead of raw Flutter primitives. Import via the barrel: `import 'package:qaswa_jewellers/core/widgets/widgets.dart';`

## Widget Reference

| Use case | Use | Instead of |
|---|---|---|
| Any text | `AppText`, `AppText.titleLarge(...)`, etc. | `Text(...)` |
| Primary action button | `AppButton(label: ..., onPressed: ...)` | `ElevatedButton` |
| Secondary/ghost button | `AppButton.outlined(...)` | `OutlinedButton` |
| Inline text-only button | `AppButton.text(...)` | `TextButton` |
| Form input | `AppTextField(label: ..., controller: ...)` | `TextFormField` / `TextField` |
| Search input | `AppSearchField(controller: ...)` | custom `TextField` with search icon |
| Dropdown / select | `AppDropdownField<T>(items: ..., onChanged: ...)` | `DropdownButton` / `DropdownButtonFormField` |
| Loading indicator | `AppLoader()` | `CircularProgressIndicator` |
| Loading inside button | pass `isLoading: true` to `AppButton` | manual loader in button child |
| Horizontal rule | `AppDivider()` | `Divider()` |
| Empty list state | `AppEmptyState(message: ...)` | custom column with icon + text |
| Error/failure state | `AppErrorState(message: ..., onRetry: ...)` | custom error column |
| Toast / feedback | `AppSnackbar.showSuccess(context, ...)` / `.showError(...)` / `.showInfo(...)` | `ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(...)` |

## AppText Named Constructors

```dart
AppText.displayLarge('Heading')
AppText.headlineMedium('Section title')
AppText.titleLarge('Card title')
AppText.titleMedium('Sub-title')
AppText.bodyLarge('Primary body')
AppText.bodyMedium('Secondary body')   // default when no constructor is used
AppText.labelLarge('Button label')
AppText.labelSmall('Caption')
```

All `AppText` variants accept optional `color`, `textAlign`, `maxLines`, and `overflow`.

## Examples

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT
AppText.titleLarge('Welcome back'),
AppText('Some body copy', color: AppColors.secondary),
AppButton(label: 'Save', onPressed: _onSave, isLoading: _isSaving),
AppButton.outlined(label: 'Cancel', onPressed: Navigator.of(context).pop),
AppTextField(label: 'Email', controller: _emailController, validator: _validateEmail),
AppDropdownField<Category>(items: categories, onChanged: _onCategorySelected),
AppSearchField(controller: _searchController, onSearch: _onSearch),
AppLoader(),
AppDivider(),
AppEmptyState(message: 'No orders yet'),
AppErrorState(onRetry: _fetchData),
AppSnackbar.showSuccess(context, 'Saved successfully'),

// ❌ WRONG — do not use raw Flutter primitives
Text('Welcome back', style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.titleLarge),
ElevatedButton(onPressed: _onSave, child: Text('Save')),
TextFormField(decoration: InputDecoration(labelText: 'Email')),
CircularProgressIndicator(),
Divider(),
ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(SnackBar(content: Text('Saved'))),
```

## ❌ Violations

- Using `Text(...)` directly anywhere in a widget tree
- Using `ElevatedButton`, `OutlinedButton`, or `TextButton` directly
- Using `TextField` or `TextFormField` directly
- Implementing a custom loading spinner instead of `AppLoader`
- Calling `showSnackBar` directly instead of `AppSnackbar`
- Building a custom empty/error state instead of `AppEmptyState` / `AppErrorState`
